  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Mobilizing local knowledge for the IYRP and engagement with UNCCD</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Central Asia&#x2019;s rangelands support biodiversity, ecosystem services and the livelihoods of millions of people. However, land degradation, climate change and unsustainable land use are placing increasing pressure on these landscapes. This activity will promote the use of local knowledge to support sustainable rangeland management and biodiversity conservation in Central Asia. It will contribute to the International Year of Rangelands and Pastoralists and support Central Asia&apos;s engagement in global discussions on sustainable land management, emphasizing the role of local knowledge in land governance.</narrative>
  </description>
